              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "When coalescing adjacent text nodes in addText and fosterParent, appending to an existing TextNode's Data via string concatenation (n.Data += text) reallocated and copied the accumulated string on every token. Inputs containing many short text runs separated by ignored end tags (such as \"a\u003c/x\u003e\") caused O(n^2) allocations and byte copies.\n\nAccumulate coalesced text in per-node byte slices during parsing and materialize Data strings once at the end of parse.",
                "text": "When coalescing adjacent text nodes in addText and fosterParent, appending to an existing TextNode's Data via string concatenation (n.Data += text) reallocated and copied the accumulated string on every token. Inputs containing many short text runs separated by ignored end tags (such as \"a\u003c/x\u003e\") caused O(n^2) allocations and byte copies.\n\nAccumulate coalesced text in per-node byte slices during parsing and materialize Data strings once at the end of parse."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-78661](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-78661)**.\n\n## [GO-2026-6860](https://osv.dev/GO-2026-6860)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e When coalescing adjacent text nodes in addText and fosterParent, appending to an existing TextNode's Data via string concatenation (n.Data += text) reallocated and copied the accumulated string on every token. Inputs containing many short text runs separated by ignored end tags (such as \"a\u003c/x\u003e\") caused O(n^2) allocations and byte copies.\n\u003e \n\u003e Accumulate coalesced text in per-node byte slices during parsing and materialize Data strings once at the end of parse.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/lewis/Desktop/devin-demo/demo-session-router/go.mod | golang.org/x/net | 0.17.0 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GO-2026-6860 | golang.org/x/net | 0.62.0 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/lewis/Desktop/devin-demo/demo-session-router/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-78661\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
