`\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-97045](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-97045)**.\n\n## [GO-2026-6866](https://osv.dev/GO-2026-6866)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e In childTextNodesAreLiteral, walking up the tree previously stopped at the nearest foreign ancestor once an HTML integration point was found. However, that integration point may itself be a descendant of an element that was foster-parented into a foreign namespace (such as \u003cmglyph\u003e or \u003cmalignmark\u003e fostered under \u003cmtext\u003e), causing a parser to resolve the subtree in a different foreign namespace upon re-parsing the rendered output.\n\u003e \n\u003e Continue walking the full ancestor chain and verify that every transition from a non-empty namespace occurs at an HTML integration point before emitting literal text.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/lewis/Desktop/devin-demo/demo-session-router/go.mod | golang.org/x/net | 0.17.0 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GO-2026-6866 | golang.org/x/net | 0.62.0 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/lewis/Desktop/devin-demo/demo-session-router/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-97045\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
